## F-GUARD-ORDER-001 - an "already running?" guard samples state too late

- **Discovered:** <YYYY-MM-DD>, <PR_OR_ITEM>
- **Symptom:** A skip-if-running, already-exists or first-time-only guard
  **always** fires, or **never** fires. It has been in the code for months and
  reads as protection in every review.
- **Root cause:** The precondition was probed **after** the guarded thing was
  created or started, so the probe observes the state the action just produced.
  The branch is dead code with a reassuring name.
- **Check:** Precondition probes sample **before** the guarded action, and the
  sample is held in a variable that the guard reads - not re-computed. Test the
  guard by **arranging the pre-existing state** and asserting the action was
  skipped; a guard tested only from a clean slate is untested.
- **Command:** `<GUARD_PRECONDITION_ORDER_TEST>`
- **Note:** a specific case of section 3's rule that an observation must not be
  read as a conclusion - here the observation is of the wrong moment.

